ts/s115.json","content":"{\n  \"is_vulnerable\": true,\n  \"cwe\": \"CWE-476\",\n  \"vulnerable_statements\": [\n    {\n      \"statement\": \"struct hv_device *hv_dev = channel->primary_channel->device_obj;\",\n      \"reason\": \"The rescind callback is invoked for primary VMBus channels, whose primary_channel pointer is always NULL (it is only set for sub-channels). Dereferencing channel->primary_channel->device_obj therefore causes a kernel NULL pointer dereference (oops/DoS) when the host rescinds the device.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"suggested_fix\": \"Get the hv_device directly from the channel being rescinded (struct hv_device *hv_dev = channel->device_obj;), since the rescind callback is only registered for primary channels. If sub-channels might ever reach this path, choose channel->primary_channel ? channel->primary_channel->device_obj : channel->device_obj, and check that hv_dev and pdata are not NULL before using them.\"\n}\n"}}}
